          "description": "Knowledge editing (KE) is an arising and promising research area that aims to alter the parameters of some specific knowledge stored in pre-trained models so that the model can make new predictions on those revised instances while keeping other irrelevant knowledge unchanged. We categorize existing methods into meta-learning, hypernetwork, and locate-and-edit -based methods.",
